MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Kai: A young boy comes of age as he fights to gain a\nnormal family life.
MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Dit: Hailing from Fódlan and heir to a legendary\nblood lust, he roams, seeking the strongest foes.
MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Seo: The dauntless queen of Saramis fights to fulfill\nher people's long-held dream.
MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Led: A rose seeks revenge, her searing songs colored\nby deep-red hatred.
MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Bel: 
MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Tal: 
MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Orh: 
MID_Obelisk_Introduction_Anh: 
MID_Obelisk_1KAI_Digest_OP: Cai is a young boy living in Ribeira with his father. They are visited by a temple\nknight who has come to tell Cai's father it's time to face punishment for\ncrimes committed before Cai's birth. Accompanied by his childhood friends,\nCai sets off for the imperial capital of Dagsion to find answers.
MID_Obelisk_1KAI_Digest_ED: Cai forges bonds with fighters who help him win the Heroic Games. He\narranges for his mother, the goddess Aurora, to meet with the Divine Sovereign\nSolel, and at last Cai's wish to live an ordinary life with his parents is granted.
MID_Obelisk_2KAI_Digest_OP: Cai is living with his parents in a rented house in the suburbs of Dagsion when\nan envoy from Saramis arrives, saying Theodora needs Cai's help. Cai quickly\ndeparts for Megaira, the capital of Saramis, to help Theodora challenge the\nmighty Dagdan Empire.
MID_Obelisk_2KAI_Digest_ED: Cai helps Theodora defeat the Divine Emperor Dagda, but the huge dragon's\nbody is sacrificed to manifest the underworld and revive the demon god Balor.\nA figure in white appears and saves Cai from certain death, and Cai manages\nto escape the ravening hordes of undead overwhelming Dagsion.
MID_Obelisk_1DIT_Digest_OP: Dietrich, an alluring swordsman descended from one of Fódlan's legendary 10\nElites, is shipwrecked in Dagda by a vast sea creature. With his Hero's Relic,\nthe fell blade Answerer, he follows his unquenchable thirst for battle to Dagsion\nin hopes of entering the Heroic Games.
MID_Obelisk_1DIT_Digest_ED: The bonds Dietrich forges with his companions change him. In the midst of his\nbattle with Mars, the Bringer of War, moved by Fabio's words—"you are\nhuman"—he resists assuming the form of a beast, instead ending the fight.\nImpressed by his skill, Mars names him the strongest human in Dagda.
MID_Obelisk_2DIT_Digest_OP: Dietrich, still in Dagsion after the conclusion of the Heroic Games, receives\nan envoy from the kingdom of Saramis. Eager to face a resurrected Dagda\nthe Great, he swiftly departs for Megaira, the kingdom's capital.
MID_Obelisk_2DIT_Digest_ED: Alongside Theodora, Dietrich defeats the dragon Dagda the Great, but the\ngod is sacrificed to manifest the underworld and revive the demon god Balor.\nA figure in white appears, saving Dietrich from certain death, and Dietrich\nbreaks free from the hellscape of Dagsion.
MID_Obelisk_1SEO_Digest_OP: Theodora returns to the royal capital of Megaira for the first time in\nyears after a tour of duty at Fort Zanbar—only for an assassin to slay her\nfather and take her right arm. Theodora searches for any path out of her\nhopeless situation, fearful of what will become of the throne of Saramis.
MID_Obelisk_1SEO_Digest_ED: Amidst concerns about her arm, and her brother Dyan's strange behavior,\nTheodora continues to fight in the Heroic Games. But when she receives word\nof Fort Zanbar's fall, she returns home immediately. Finding that her brother\nworked with the Mosa to overthrow her, she defeats Dyan to end his rebellion.
MID_Obelisk_2SEO_Digest_OP: After her victory at Fort Zanbar, Theodora busies herself with post-battle\nmatters when astonishing news arrives: the Divine Emperor Dagda has been\nrevived and declared war on the kingdom of Saramis. In response, Theodora\nmobilizes her allies, spurring them to march on Dagsion.
MID_Obelisk_2SEO_Digest_ED: Theodora marches into Dagsion to deliver a final defeat to the Divine\nEmperor, but the huge dragon's body is sacrificed to manifest the underworld\nand revive the demon god Balor. A figure in white appears, saving Theodora\nfrom certain death, and she escapes the undead hordes swarming over Dagsion.
MID_Obelisk_1LED_Digest_OP: Leda is on a quest for revenge, seeking to kill those named in a list left by her\nmentor Mahdel before he died. After discovering that her father's murderer is\nstill alive, she enters the Heroic Games so that she may finally kill him.\nThere's no telling where this bloody journey may bring her.
MID_Obelisk_1LED_Digest_ED: Although Leda defeats Bertrand in the Heroic Games, she does not take his life.\nShe realizes her true enemy is someone else, whom she can't fight on her own.\nEntrusting the investigation to the Divine Sovereign, Leda intends to travel\nsouth and discover some way to save her father's soul from the underworld.
MID_Obelisk_2LED_Digest_OP: At the temple of Kalla, Leda is preparing to travel, but her plans abruptly\nchange when an envoy from the kingdom of Saramis arrives. Leda's fierce\nresentment for the Divine Emperor leads her to depart for Megaira, the\nkingdom's capital, to help Theodora challenge the mighty Dagdan Empire.
MID_Obelisk_2LED_Digest_ED: Alongside Theodora, Leda defeats Dagda the Great, but the huge dragon's\nbody is sacrificed to manifest the underworld and revive the demon god Balor.\nA figure in white appears, saving Leda from certain death, and she escapes the\nundead hordes swarming over Dagsion.
