MID_Obelisk_3ISM_c01_Digest: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} has toiled in the Obelisk Chamber that Fortuna, Goddess of\nFate, prepared for them. Now, they have emerged into Dagsion, which has\nbecome an underworld city bereft of the living. Their task is to destroy the\nunderworld gates and free the world from the forces of the demon god Balor.
MID_Obelisk_3ISM_c02_Digest: After {AvatarName} defeats Brimstone Lord Dagda and liberates\nDagsion, people come from all over the continent seeking refuge.\n{AvatarName}'s mission to destroy the gates of the underworld across\nthe land and defeat the demon god Balor enters a new phase.
MID_Obelisk_3ISM_c03_Digest: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} defeats the strength-obsessed Brimstone Lord Breza,\nbut the war only grows more pitched. Amidst the clash between the living\nand the risen dead, whose thirst to kill recognizes no bonds, Fortuna\nspeaks of the truth behind Balor's rebellion against the progenitor god.
MID_Obelisk_3ISM_c04_Digest: Even rulers of the world are seen swallowed by the darkness, but such is the\nimmutable law of flux governing humanity since before the underworld\nmanifested. As the war with the dead rages on, Fortuna tells {AvatarName}\nof the temple of the Diadem, in which greater power may be found.
MID_Obelisk_3ISM_c05_Digest: A former king cloaked in deceit, and a man whose heart is consumed with\npride... The chaos intensifies as the battles with the Brimstone Lords are akin to\nconfrontations with karma itself. Fortuna speaks of a destined end that even\nthe gods cannot escape and suggests that this spurs all to live life to its fullest.
MID_Obelisk_3ISM_c06_Digest: More Brimstone Lords guard the gates of the underworld, each with\ntheir own karma. After a series of difficult battles, {AvatarName}\nstrides toward the final confrontation. Beyond the last underworld gate\nwaits Balor. The battle for the fate of humanity is about to begin.
MID_Obelisk_HowToPlay_Kai: <DLG>Cai is a pure-hearted, energetic boy who shares a bond with animals.\n\nSince he's still a boy, he is not allowed to venture into some locales,\nbut he can gather materials, farm for crops, and capture ridable\nanimals for his companions to use in mounted combat.\n\nBy helping people in the city solve their problems, he will grow his\nrenown and receive mentoring from more experienced fighters.
MID_Obelisk_HowToPlay_Dit: <DLG>Dietrich, a fearsome swordsman, seeks battle for pleasure.\n\nHe can challenge the strongest of wandering warriors by using his fell\nblade to locate them and may also be challenged by foes from across\nthe land. By defeating them, he can make their combat arts his own.\n\nOnce obtained in battle, these combat arts may be strengthened or\ntaught to his comrades at the temple, allowing him to bolster his clan.
MID_Obelisk_HowToPlay_Seo: <DLG>Theodora, known by some as the Iron Bastion, is the queen of Saramis.\n\nShe can recruit soldiers from settlements she visits to bring them under\nher banner as battalions. Assigning a battalion to a unit increases\ntheir power in battle and allows the use of their special gambits.\n\nShe can also deploy battalions to locations on the map to gather\nresources for her, allowing them to aid the queen outside of combat.
MID_Obelisk_HowToPlay_Led: <DLG>Leda, who holds the title of Rose of Caelus, excels in the arts.\n\nBy accepting quests and performing at local taverns, she can learn\nnew spellsongs, as well as gain certification in the dancer class.\n\nMoreover, she has access to purchasing special drinks that grant\nvarious benefits, and she can learn about hidden locations.